# Line endings. Every text file is checked out exactly as it is committed,
# with LF, on every system. A Windows runner (or a Windows clone) has
# core.autocrlf on, and the tests read sources, docs, workflows, the
# release notes and the frozen answers byte for byte, so a checkout that
# turned LF into CRLF failed them with nothing wrong in the code. Every
# file in the repository was LF when this was added, so nothing committed
# changes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary by type: never converted, whatever git's guess. A PDF in
# particular reads as text to git's heuristic and was being rewritten.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff2 binary
*.epub binary
*.mobi binary
*.azw3 binary
*.kfx binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.bin binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.localstorage binary

# Data compared byte for byte, text or not: the committed fixtures (which
# tests/fixture-stability regenerates and compares), the frozen answers
# beside each crate's tests, and the oracle (which has its own file too).
tests/fixtures/** -text
rust/crates/*/tests/data/** -text
rust/oracle/** -text
